## Always Do First
- **Invoke the `frontend-design` skill** before writing any frontend code, every session, no exceptions.
- **Read `brand_assets/theme.json`** before writing any styles — all design decisions must come from it.
- **Invoke the `tallores-integration` skill** for any reservation-related work.

## Template Architecture

This project is a **multi-restaurant template**. `index.html` contains zero brand-specific content — it is a pure rendering shell. All brand data lives in `brand_assets/`.

```
brand_assets/
  content.json   ← ALL text, nav, contact, images paths
  theme.json     ← ALL design tokens (colors, fonts, spacing, shadows)
  logo.svg       ← restaurant logo (or logo.png)
  *.jpg / *.png  ← photos
  menu.pdf       ← menu (optional — if present, a Menu section is shown)
```

**To rebrand this site for a different restaurant:** replace the entire `brand_assets/` folder. The HTML and JS do not change.

### How it works

`index.html` fetches both JSONs on load:
1. `initTheme(theme)` — writes all `theme.json` values as CSS custom properties on `:root`
2. `renderPage(content)` — populates every DOM node from `content.json`

All colors in CSS use `var(--color-*)`. All fonts use `var(--font-heading)` / `var(--font-body)`. No hex values appear in `index.html`.

### Adding new styled elements

- **New color or font** → add to `theme.json` first, then reference via the CSS custom property it maps to.
- **New content** → add to `content.json`, then add a renderer call in `renderPage()`.
- Never hard-code brand values directly in `index.html`.

### Key content.json sections

| Key | Purpose |
|-----|---------|
| `meta` | `<title>` and `<meta description>` |
| `restaurant` | Name, tagline, hero subtitle, story text |
| `assets` | Logo path, image paths |
| `nav` | Nav link labels/hrefs, CTA button |
| `menu_pdf` | Path to menu PDF (omit key if no PDF) |
| `contact` | Address, phone, email, hours |
| `footer` | Address line, copyright |

## Local Server
- Start the dev server: `node serve.mjs` (serves the project root at `http://localhost:3000`)
- `serve.mjs` lives in the project root. Start it in the background.
- If the server is already running, do not start a second instance.

## Output Defaults
- Single `index.html` file, all styles inline
- Tailwind CSS via CDN: `<script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>`
- Mobile-first responsive

## Brand Assets
- `brand_assets/` contains: `theme.json`, `content.json`, logo, photos, and optionally `menu.pdf`
- Use real assets — do not use placeholders where real assets are available.

## Anti-Generic Guardrails
- **Colors:** Never use default Tailwind palette (indigo-500, blue-600, etc.). All colors from `theme.json`.
- **Shadows:** Never use flat `shadow-md`. Use layered, color-tinted shadows from `theme.json`.
- **Typography:** Heading font paired with body font from `theme.json`. Apply tight tracking on large headings, generous line-height on body.
- **Animations:** Only animate `transform` and `opacity`. Never `transition-all`. Use spring-style easing.
- **Interactive states:** Every clickable element needs hover, focus-visible, and active states.
- **Images:** Add warm overlay on images. Add gradient overlay on hero images.
- **Spacing:** Use spacing tokens from `theme.json`.

## Reservation Widget (TalloRes)
- **Invoke the `tallores-integration` skill** for any reservation-related work — widget placement, nav link wiring, URL construction.
- The TalloRes RestaurantId is stored as `<meta name="tallores-restaurant-id">` in `<head>`.

## Hard Rules
- Do not use `transition-all`
- Do not use default Tailwind blue/indigo as primary color
- Do not introduce a color, font, size, or shadow not present in `theme.json` — add it there first
